A two-cluster Edge matrix that this scheduler accepts and whose steal rule works.

The matrix is built when the CPU driver calls ml_cpu_init_completed (ArmCpu, boot argument armcpu-edge=1). Without the
call every edge stays closed: no thread moves between the E cluster (three A510 cores) and the P cluster, in either
direction. The macOS boot arguments do not carry the argument. In runs 56 to 61 the busiest E core was at 90 % or more
in 13 to 28 % of the 10 s rows, and in run 61 the busiest core of cpu3 to cpu6 was at 60 % or less in 10 of those 12
rows ([cpu gov]).

The matrix the board patch builds does not do what it says on this kernel:
- P -> E is closed for the fixed priority, foreground and user-initiated buckets and open for default and lower. The
  scheduler requires an edge to be at least as open for a higher bucket as for a lower one
  (sched_edge_config_verify_non_decreasing_qos_strictness; its searches stop at the first closed bucket), so the check
  fails.
- E -> P allows stealing without migration, for an idle P core to take E work. The steal search admits a cluster's
  threads only when the fixed priority bucket of that edge may migrate (scr_incoming_migration_allowed,
  sched_edge_pset_peek_steal_possible), so a P core never takes them.

Here P -> E is closed for every bucket, so a thread that prefers P runs on P as it does today. E -> P allows stealing
for every bucket with the weight of a weighted spill (a steal then needs more runnable threads than E cores) and
migration for the fixed priority bucket alone, which opens the steal search and moves nothing: no thread group prefers
E for that bucket.

Two counters, each with index 0 for the E and 1 for the P cluster type: sheng_edge_cross_type_steals counts the threads
a cluster took from the run queues of the other type, and sheng_edge_idle_beside_excess counts the times a core found
nothing to run while the other type had more runnable threads than cores. The second works with the matrix unbuilt:
against the idle entries of cpu3 to cpu7 it says how often a P core went idle beside waiting E work.

Applies after zzyf-sheng-amp.patch and zzzz-sheng-ipados27-bringup.patch. Has not run on hardware.
